message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on Descendants costumes. The jumpsuit is a flimsy costume of textile material, so it is likely classified as a festive article under 9505.90.6000 (HTSUS), or as wearing apparel under chapter 61 if it is of a quality that qualifies as apparel. The flimsy construction, loose overlock stitching, and lack of modesty are the usual CBP reasons for treating a costume as a festive article rather than apparel.

The second item is a jacket, belt, earrings and fingerless gloves set. It is likely a set classified under a single heading, and the rulings often treat such sets as festive articles too. A single code is needed, and 9505.90.6000 covers both items.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The jumpsuit and the dress-up set are flimsy, loosely stitched costume items that lack the quality of wearing apparel, so they are classified as festive articles in heading 9505, other, under 9505.90.6000."}
